According to the law of conservation of momentum,

\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{P}_{\text {(initial) }}=\mathrm{P}_{\text {(final) }} \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{mu}_{1}+\mathrm{Mu}_{2}=\mathrm{mv}_{1}+\mathrm{Mv}_{2} \\
\Rightarrow 0+0=10 \times 10 \times 10^{-3} \times 800+[100-10 \times
\left.10 \times 10^{-3}\right] \mathrm{v}
\end{array}

\Rightarrow \mathrm{v}=\frac{-800}{999} \Rightarrow-0.8 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}

Negative sign indicates that the velocity is opposite to the direction of bullets.

Using principle of conservation of linear momentum,
$\begin{array}{l}
3 \mathrm{~m} \times \mathrm{v}=\sqrt{(\mathrm{m} \times 60)^{2}+(\mathrm{m} \times 60)^{2}} \\
=\mathrm{m} \times 60 \sqrt{2} \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{v}=20 \sqrt{2} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}
\end{array}$

After collision the bullet and block move together and comes to rest after covering a distance of $40 \mathrm{~m}$.
